id=mt6639-hotspot
name=MT6639 Native EHT Hotspot
version=v0.2.22
versionCode=30
author=mt6639-dijun
description=v0.2.22 adds the terminal judgement to the recovery report: when the native runner has already exited, no mtap0 exists, the driver is back and the station verifies, the access point counts as torn down even if a step that had nothing left to do returned non-zero; the original code is kept in recovery.note. v0.2.21 stops replaying a recorded recovery failure: start/stop now retry the checked recovery itself (at most 2 per boot, 20s cooldown, each failed result archived as recovery.failed.N) so a single transient error no longer locks the module until reboot. v0.2.20 gives the post-teardown station check a bounded retry (8 x 3s) before falling back to select: the AP teardown makes Android re-associate the STA, and checking the instant the interface disappears lost that race, so select disconnected a connection that was still coming up and its 20s verification window expired (false station_state=selection_failed / recovery_rc=1 seen on device). v0.2.19 no longer fails a 6GHz start when the STA is on a different 6GHz node of the same SSID: auto still resolves to wifi, the BSSID/channel pin mismatches, and the runner now downgrades to wifi-any (uplink over wlan0, identity unasserted) and records the real STA frequency in upstream.note, instead of exiting with sta_upstream_mismatch. Every other pin mismatch still fails closed. v0.2.18 refreshes the Android runtime environment when system_server changed (soft reboot), because long-lived KernelSU services kept a stale BOOTCLASSPATH and app_process then aborted inside artInitializeStaticStorageFromCode with no output — previously reported as reason=unreported. The runner now re-sources android-env.sh on every start and names that failure as framework_inspect_failed with the app_process status and stderr. v0.2.17 pins the LabNet-2.4G upstream to the AP's real BSSID (02:00:00:00:73:1a) and fixes the guardian band inheritance that made a 5g teardown look for reconnect.key instead of reconnect-2g.key. v0.2.16 makes 2.4GHz a first-class native profile: start 2g 20 renders an HE-only BSS (hw_mode=g, op_class=81, 2437MHz/ch6, ieee80211n=1 ieee80211ax=1, no VHT/EHT IEs), the runner drives ApEHT=0 for that band and restores the measured prior value, STATUS must report ieee80211n=1 ieee80211ax=1 ieee80211be=0 before success, and a 2.4GHz STA upstream is refused (sta_band_incompatible_with_2g). v0.2.15 exports the Android runtime environment for service.sh, action.sh, the Settings worker and the native runner. Experimental explicit-action hotspot lifecycle; disabled by default; supports 6GHz EHT plus 5GHz and 2.4GHz HE profiles, checked stop/recovery, a read-only Settings status/readiness snapshot, a fixed-argument Settings bridge, and root-private first-install worker initialization.
